                     The Manifesto
============================================================

Any content on this website is free to take! All information
and opinions and programs are subject to change at any time.
Reader beware. Nate is a dumbass and occasionally makes some
mistakes. Critically evaluate the information on this site.


                     The Organization
============================================================

Write a post in ./posts/ (Typst) that starts with a meta block:

    #let meta = (
      title: "Convex Functions",
      date: "1-7-26",
      summary: "Brief coverage of convex functions.",
    )

and it appears on the site as /convex_functions.html, listed on
the home page (`listed: false` publishes the page but leaves it
off). Unfinished posts go in ./drafts/, which is committed and
pushed but never built or published; to publish one, move it
into ./posts/ (git mv drafts/x.typ posts/).

Before every push, hooks/pre-push builds the site and looks for
leftover merge-conflict markers. If either fails the push stops
and the error is printed with its file and line. Running
./build.sh once switches this on in each clone; skip it once
with `git push --no-verify`.

./index.typ    the home page bio and links
./theme.typ    page chrome and helpers (#hr) shared by posts
./site.typ     ties it together: finds the posts, builds every page
./fonts/       New Computer Modern Math (GUST Font License), the
               math font of Typst's PDFs, from typst-assets 0.15.1

Netlify runs ./build.sh on every push and publishes ./_site/,
so generated HTML is never committed. Locally (typst >= 0.15):

    ./build.sh                 build the site into ./_site/
    ./build.sh watch           rebuild ./_site/ on every save
    ./build.sh pdf FILE.typ    live PDF preview of a post or draft


